From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amirali Abdolrashidi <abdolrashidi@google.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:29:01 -0700
Subject: Vulkan: Sync dirty disabled active attributes

  Currently when a vertex array is being synced at draw, it only
sets the disabled inactive attributes to empty buffer. However,
in cases, if an attribute is disabled after a draw call and there
is a multidraw call with zero counts, it does not sync the attribute
correctly due to the cleanup being deferred, which is skipped entirely
when the multidraw is treated as a no-op later. This leads to the
backend keeping the pointer for the data buffer, even if it is freed
before the next draw call, which can lead to use-after-free errors.

This change makes sure even the active disabled attributes are also
synced to empty buffers, removing the UAF risk.

* Updated VertexArrayVk::syncState() so syncDirtyDisabledAttribs()
  is used for disabled active attributes as well as inactive ones.

* Added unit tests to MultiDrawTest:
  * StaleSlot*WithSameLocations
  * StaleSlot*WithDifferentLocations

  * Each draws with a program, disables one of its attributes, then
    multidraws with 0 vertices, switches to another similar program,
    deletes the buffer corresponding to the disabled attributes, and
    draws. The tests should not crash.

Bug: chromium:573933450
Bug: chromium:571059182
Change-Id: I69f89addc8b500398c488c1e2ddc4d67c3505066
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8666698
Commit-Queue: Amirali Abdolrashidi <abdolrashidi@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Charlie Lao <cclao@google.com>

